                <pb facs="0548" n="474" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg474"/>


                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Prince Kung to Mr.
                        Williams</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="chinese-era chinese-lunisolar gregorian" when="1866-09-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#small-caps">September</hi> 26, 1866, (<hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Tungchi</hi> 4<hi rendition="#italic">th
                                year</hi>, 8<hi rendition="#italic">th moon,</hi> 7<hi
                                rendition="#italic">th day.</hi>)</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Prince Kung, chief secretary of state for foreign affairs, herewith makes a
                    communication:</p>
                <p>I have recently consulted with M. de Bellouet, French chargé d’affaires,
                    respecting a modification of that part of Article XXII of the treaty with France
                    which relates to the levying of tonnage dues, and have settled the alterations
                    to be made in it. I accordingly now enclose a copy of the amended portion of the
                    article.</p>
                <p>It has been decided that at Ningpo and all the open ports north of it the
                    regulation shall come into effect on the 15th of October, and at Fuhchau and
                    parts south of it on the 1st of November next.</p>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wells Williams</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Chargé d’ Affaires.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
